---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---

<Base
  title="Code of Conduct"
  description="ROS Guangzhou community code of conduct: shared rules for offline events and online group chats."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Code of Conduct</h1>
    <p>Applies to ROSGZ offline events, online group chats and this site's collaboration spaces.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What we expect</h2>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li>
      <div class="title">1. Critique the work, not the person</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Discuss code, designs and conclusions. When pointing out a mistake, provide verifiable evidence where you
        can.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="title">2. Respect different levels of experience</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Beginner questions are not noise. "I read the docs and still don't get it" deserves a real answer —
        and beginners should describe what they have already tried.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="title">3. No unwelcome promotion</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Do not sell courses, hardware or outsourcing in the group or at events. Job postings are allowed, but no
        spamming and no disguising ads as technical discussion.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="title">4. Zero tolerance for harassment</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Harassment of any kind (verbal, sexual innuendo, personal attacks, photographing or sharing without
        consent) is unacceptable, including derogatory remarks about gender, sexual orientation, appearance,
        ethnicity, religion, disability, skill level or employer.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="title">5. Respect venues and other people's equipment</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Do not move others' hardware, connect to their networks or run risky operations on site without
        permission. Any live-robot demo must be assessed by its presenter with e-stop and isolation prepared.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="title">6. Ask before photographing or publishing</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Events may be photographed or recorded. If you do not want to appear in public material, tell the
        organizers on the spot and we will avoid or blur you.
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting and handling</h2>
  <p>
    If any of the above is violated, contact the organizers or any volunteer through the channels listed on the
    <a href={url('/en/join')}>Join</a> page, and share the time, setting and any evidence you have.
  </p>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li>
      <div class="title">How we handle it</div>
      <div class="desc">
        Organizers verify privately and protect the reporter's identity; when necessary we ask the person to leave
        an event or the group. For serious violations (violence, harassment, fraud) the person is not invited back.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="title">Honest limits</div>
      <div class="desc">
        The community is volunteer-run, so we cannot promise a fixed response time. If there is a risk to personal
        safety or a possible crime, please contact the police or seek legal help first.
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Provenance:</strong> this code follows the core principles of widely used open-source codes of conduct
    (such as the Contributor Covenant) and is rewritten for this local community. It does not reproduce any
    licensed text verbatim, so no verbatim applicability of such documents is claimed here.
  </div>
</Base>
